// Title: Wdigest CredGuard Registry Modification
// Sigma ID: 1a2d6c47-75b0-45bd-b133-2c0be75349fd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2019-08-25 | Modified: 2021-11-27
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects potential malicious modification of the property value of IsCredGuardEnabled from
//   HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\SecurityProviders\WDigest to disable Cred Guard on a
//   system. This is usually used with UseLogonCredential to manipulate the caching credentials.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://teamhydra.blog/2020/08/25/bypassing-credential-guard/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_disable_wdigest_credential_guard.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\IsCredGuardEnabled"
